{
  "title": "First ten days of Zilhajj",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Salaat between Maghrib and Isha\nAt each of these ten nights, it is recommended to offer a two unit prayer between the Maghrib and Isha’ obligatory prayers and to recite at each unit [Surah al-Faatehah](A5) once, [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) once, and the following verse (7/142):\nوَ وَاعَدْنَا مُوْسٰى ثَلَاثِيْنَ لَيْلَةً \nWA WAA-A’DNAA MOOSAA SALAASEENA LAYLATAN\nAnd We appointed with Moses a time of thirty nights \nوَ اَتْمَمْنَاهَا بِعَشْرٍ \nWA ATMAMNAAHAA BE-A’SHRIN\nand completed them with ten more, \nفَتَمَّ مِيْقَاتُ رَبِّهٖ اَرْبَعِيْنَ لَيْلَةً\nFA-TAMMA MEEQAATO RABBEHI ARBA-E’ENA LAYLATAN\nso the appointed time of his Lord was complete forty nights, \nوَ قَالَ مُوْسٰى لِاَخِيْهِ هَارُوْنَ\nWA QAALA MOOSAA LE-AKHEEHE HAAROONAKH\nand Moses said to his brother Aaron: \nاخْلُفْنِيْ فِيْ قَوْمِيْ وَ اَصْلِحْ\nLUFNEE FEE QAWMEE WA ASLEH\nTake my place among my people, and act well \nوَ لَا تَتَّبِعْ سَبِيْلَ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ.\nWA LAA TATTA-BE’ SABEELAL MUFSEDEEN.\nand do not follow the way of the mischief-makers.\nThe reward of offering this prayer is to participate in the rewards of those who go on Hajj.",
  "merits": "Introduction\nIn the blessed month of Zilhajj, the pious companions of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and their followers used to do acts of worship extraordinarily. The first ten days of this month are called al-ayyam al-ma’lumat (The Stated Days) by the Holy Qur’an.\nAbout these highly honorable days, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) is reported to have said that nothing is more preferable to Almighty Allah than practicing acts of worship on these ten stated days.\nIt is recommended to observe fasting on the first nine days of Zilhajj, for it is equal to the fasting of one’s whole lifetime.\nThe 8th Day Of Zilhajj is called the Tarwiyah Day. To observe fasting on this day brings about a great reward. According to a narration, it erases the sins of sixty years. Shaykh al-Shahid (the martyr) has said that it is recommended to bathe oneself on this day.",
  "tabs": [
    "Dua after Fajr and Before Magrib\nIt is recommended to say the following supplicatory prayer, which is reported by Shaykh al-Tusi and Sayyid Ibn Tawus from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.), after the obligatory Fajr and Maghrib Prayers since the first day of Zilhajj and up to the eve of the ‘Arafat Night, the ninth of Zilhajj:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ هٰذِهِ الْاَيَّامُ الَّتِيْ \nALLAAHUMMA HAAZEHIL AYYAAMUL LATEE\nO Allah, these days that \nفَضَّلْتَهَا عَلَى الْاَيَّامِ وَ شَرَّفْتَهَا \nFAZZALTAHAA A'LAL AYYAAME WA SHARRAFTAHAA \nYou have preferred and favored on other days, \nقَدْ بَلَّغْتَنِيْهَا بِمَنِّكَ وَ رَحْمَتِكَ\nQAD BALLAGHTANEEHAA BEMANNEKA WA RAHMATEKA \nYou have allowed me to attain them out of Your favor and mercy; \nفَاَنْزِلْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ بَرَكَاتِكَ\nFA-ANZIL A'LAYNAA MIN BARAKAATEKA \nso, (please) descend on us Your blessings \nوَ اَوْسِعْ عَلَيْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ نَعْمَاۤئِكَ\nWA AW-SEA' A'LAYNAA FEEHAA MIN NA'MAAA-EKA \nand expand for us Your boons. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA AN TOSALLEYA A'LAA MOHAMMADIWN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nO Allah, I beseech you to send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad \nوَ اَنْ تَهْدِيَنَا فِيْهَا لِسَبِيْلِ الْهُدٰى\nWA AN TAHDEYANAA FEEHAA LESABEELIL HODAA \nand to guide us on these days to the path of guidance, \nوَ الْعَفَافِ وَ الْغِنٰى\nWAL A'FAAFE WAL GHENAA \nchastity, sufficiency, \nوَ الْعَمَلِ فِيْهَا بِمَا تُحِبُّ وَ تَرْضٰىۤ\nWAL A'MALE FEEHAA BEMAA TOHIBBO WA TARZAA \nand doing that which You like and please. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ يَا مَوْضِعَ كُلِّ شَكْوٰى \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOKA YAA MAWZE-A' KULLE SHAKWAA \nO Allah, I beseech You, O object of all complaints, \nوَ يَا سَامِعَ كُلِّ نَجْوٰى\nWA YAA SAAME-A' KULLE NAJWAA \nO Hearer of all confidential talks, \nوَ يَا شَاهِدَ كُلِّ مَلَاٍ \nWA YAA SHAAHEDA KULLE MALAA-IN \nO Attendant in all sessions, \nوَ يَا عَالِمَ كُلِّ خَفِيَّةٍ\nWA YAA A'ALEMA KULLE KHAFIYYATIN \nO Knower of all hidden matters, \nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nAN TOSALLEYA A'LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nto send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, \nوَ اَنْ تَكْشِفَ عَنَّا فِيْهَا الْبَلَاۤءَ \nWA AN TAKSHEFA A'NNAA FEEHAL BALAAA-A \nrelieve us from all hardships on these days, \nوَ تَسْتَجِيْبَ لَنَا فِيْهَا الدُّعَاۤءَ\nWA TASTAJEEBA LANAA FEEHAD DO-A'AA-A \nrespond to our prayers, \nوَ تُقَوِّيَنَا فِيْهَا وَ تُعِيْنَنَا \nWA TOQAWWEYANAA FEEHAA WA TO-E'ENANAA \ngrant us power, aid us, \nوَ تُوَفِّقَنَا فِيْهَا لِمَا تُحِبُّ رَبَّنَا وَ تَرْضٰى\nWA TOWAFFEQANAA FEEHAA LEMAA TOHIBBO RABBANAA WA TARZAA \nand lead us successfully to all that which You, \nوَ عَلٰى مَا افْتَرَضْتَ عَلَيْنَا \nWA A'LAA MAF TARAZTA A'LAYNAA \nO our Lord, like and please and to do acts of\nمِنْ طَاعَتِكَ وَ طَاعَةِ رَسُوْلِكَ \nMIN TAA-A'TEKA WA TAA-A'TE RASOOLEKA \nobedience to You that which You have made obligatory upon us as well as acts of obedience to Your Messenger \nوَ اَهْلِ وِلَايَتِكَ\nWA AHLE WELAAYATEKA \nand to the men of Your leadership. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيْۤ اَسْاَلُكَ يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ \nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS-ALOK YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA \nO Allah, I beseech You, O most Merciful of all those who show mercy, \nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAN TOSALLEYA A'LAA MOHAMMADINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nto send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad \nوَ اَنْ تَهَبَ لَنَا فِيْهَا الرِّضَا\nWA AN TAHABA LANAA FEEHAR REZAA \nand grant us [Your] pleasure on these days. \nاِنَّكَ سَمِيْعُ الدُّعَاۤءِ \nINNAKA SAMEE-U'D DO-A'AA-E \nYou are verily Hearer of prayers. \nوَ لَا تَحْرِمْنَا خَيْرَ مَا تُنْزِلُ فِيْهَا مِنَ السَّمَاۤءِ\nWA LAA TAHRIMNAA KHAYRA MAA TUNZELO FEEHAA MENAS SAMAAA-E \nDo not deprive us of the good that You cause to come down from the heavens on these days, \nوَ طَهِّرْنَا مِنَ الذُّنُوْبِ\nWA TAHHIRNAA MENAZ ZONOOBE \npurify us from sins, \nيَا عَلَّامَ الْغُيُوْبِ\nYAA A'LLAAMAL GHOYOOBE \nO Knower of all unseen things, \nوَ اَوْجِبْ لَنَا فِيْهَا دَارَ الْخُلُوْدِ \nWA AWJIB LANAA FEEHAA DAARAL KHOLOODE \nand make certain for us the abode of immortality. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nALLAAHUMMA SALLE A'LAA MOHAMMAHDINW WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \nO Allah, send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad \nوَ لَا تَتْرُكْ لَنَا فِيْهَا ذَنْبًا اِلَّا غَفَرْتَهٗ \nWA LAA TATRUK LANAA FEEHAA ZANBAN ILLAA GHAFARTAHU \nand do not leave for us a sin but that You forgive it, \nوَ لَا هَمًّا اِلَّا فَرَّجْتَهٗ \nWA LAA HAMMAN ILLAA FARRAJTAHU \nno depression but that You relieve it, \nوَ لَا دَيْنًا اِلَّا قَضَيْتَهٗ \nWA DAYNAN ILLAA QAZAYTAHU \nno debt but that You help us settle it, \nوَ لَا غَاۤئِبًا اِلَّاۤ اَدَّيْتَهٗ \nWA LAA GHAAA-EBAN ILLAA ADDAYTAHU \nno absent but that You make join us, \nوَ لَا حَاجَةً مِنْ حَوَاۤئِجِ الدُّنْيَا وَ الْاٰخِرَةِ \nWA LAA HAAJATAN MIN HAWAA-EJID DUNYAA WAL AAAKHERATE \nand no need in this world and the Next World \nاِلَّا سَهَّلْتَهَا وَ يَسَّرْتَهَا \nILLAA SAHHALTAHAA WA YASSARTAHAA \nbut that You make it easy and obtainable. \nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ \nINNAKA A'LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN \nYou, verily, have power over all things. \nاَللّٰهُمَّ يَا عَالِمَ الْخَفِيَّاتِ \nALLAAHUMMA YAA A'ALEMAL KHAFIYYAATE \nO Allah! O Knower of all hidden things! \nيَا رَاحِمَ الْعَبَرَاتِ يَا مُجِيْبَ الدَّعَوَاتِ \nYAA RAAHEMAL A'BARAATE YAA MOJEEBAD DA'WAATE \nO Merciful of all tears! O Answerer of all prayers! \nيَا رَبَّ الْاَرَضِيْنَ وَ السَّمَاوَاتِ \nYAA RABBAL ARAZEENA WAS SAMAAWAATE \nO Lord of the [layers of the] earth and the heavens! \nيَا مَنْ لَا تَتَشَابَهٗ عَلَيْهِ الْاَصْوَاتُ \nYAA MAN LAA TATASHAABAHU A'LAYHIL ASWAATO \nO He Who is not confused by various sounds! \nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ \nSALLE A'LAA MOHAMMADIWN WA AALE MOHAMMADIN \n(Please) send blessings to Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad \nوَ اجْعَلْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ عُتَقَاۤئِكَ \nWAJ A'LNAA FEEHAA MIN O'TAQAAA-EKA \nand include us, on these days, with those whom You release \nوَ طُلَقَاۤئِكَ مِنَ النَّارِ \nWA TOLA-QAAA-EKA MENAN NAARE \nand discharge from Hellfire, \nوَ الْفَاۤئِزِيْنَ بِجَنَّتِكَ وَ النَّاجِيْنَ \nWAL FAAA-EZEENA BEJANNATEKA WAN NAAJEENA \nthose whom You make win Your Paradise, and those whom You save, \nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ \nBERAHMATEKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHEMEENA \nout of Your mercy. O most Merciful of all those who show mercy! \nوَ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى سَيِّدِنَا مُحَمَّدٍ وَ اٰلِهٖ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWA SALLAL LAAHO A'LAA SAYYEDENA MOHAMMADINW WA AALEHI AJMA-E'ENA.\nAllah may send blessings to our master, Muhammad, and to his entire Household.",
    "Five Tasbeeh\nIt is recommended to say the following five testaments on the first ten days of Zilhajj:\n(1) اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ \nASH-HADO AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU \nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner. \nلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَ لَهُ الْحَمْدُ بِيَدِهِ الْخَيْرُ \nLAHUL MULKO WA LAHUL HAMDO BEYADEHIL KHAYRO \nHis is the kingdom and His is all praise. In His Hand is all goodness, \nوَ هُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ \nWA HOWA A'LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN.\nand He has power over all things. \n (2) اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADO AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU \nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner. \nاَحَدًا صَمَدًا لَمْ يَتَّخِذْ صَاحِبَةً وَّ لَا وَلَدًا \nAHADAN SAMADAN LAM YATTAKHIZ SAAHEBATAN WA LAA WALADAN.\nOne and Only and Besought of all. He has not taken to Himself wife nor son. \n(3) اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ \nASH-HADO AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU \nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner, \nاَحَدًا صَمَدًا لَمْ يَلِدْ وَ لَمْ يُوْلَدْ وَ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهٗ كُفُوًا اَحَدٌ \nAHADAN SAMADAN LAM YALID WA LAM YOOLAD WA LAM YAKUN LAHU KOFOWAN AHADUN.\nOne and Only and Besought of all. He begets not, nor is He begotten, and there is none comparable to Him. \n(4) اَشْهَدُ اَنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَحْدَهٗ لَا شَرِيْكَ لَهٗ\nASH-HADO AN LAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WAHDAHU LAA SHAREEKA LAHU \nI bear witness that there is no god save Allah, alone without having any partner. \nلَهُ الْمُلْكُ وَ لَهُ الْحَمْدُ يُحْيِيْ وَ يُمِيْتُ\nLAHUL MULKO WA LAHUL HAMDO YOHYEE WA YOMEETO \nHis is the kingdom and His is all praise. He brings to life and causes to die, \nوَ هُوَ حَيٌّ لَا يَمُوْتُ بِيَدِهِ الْخَيْرُ وَ هُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْ‏ءٍ قَدِيْرٌ \nWA HOWA HAYYUN LAA YAMOOTO BEYADEHIL KHAYRO WA HOWA A'LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEERUN.\nand He is Ever-living and never dies. In His Hand is all goodness and He has power over all things. \n(5) حَسْبِيَ اللّٰهُ وَ كَفٰى سَمِعَ اللّٰهُ لِمَنْ دَعَا\nHASBEYAL LAAHO WA KAFAA SAME-A'L LAAHO LEMAN DA-A'A \nSufficient to me is Allah and nothing else. May Allah listen from him who prays to Him. \nلَيْسَ وَرَاۤءَ اللّٰهِ مُنْتَهٰى اَشْهَدُ لِلّٰهِ بِمَا دَعَا\nLAYSA WARAAA-AL LAAHE MUNTAHAA ASH-HADO LILLAAHE BEMAA DA-A'AA \nThere is no end beyond Allah. I bear witness to Allah for all that He has declared, \nوَ اَنَّهٗ بَرِيْۤ‏ءٌ مِمَّنْ تَبَرَّاَ وَ اَنَّ لِلّٰهِ الْاٰخِرَةَ وَ الْاُوْلٰى.\nWA ANNAHU BAREE-UN MIMMAN TABARRA-A WA ANNA LILLAAHIL AAKHERATO WAL OOLAA.\nHe is clear of all that from which He has declared clearness, and Allah’s is the end and the beginning of all things.\nArchangel Gabriel has conveyed these five testaments as gift of Almighty Allah to Prophet Jesus (a.s.) and instructed him to say them on the first ten days of Zilhajj.\nAn excellent reward has been mentioned to be for whoever repeats these five statements one hundred times each day. However, ‘Allamah al-Majlisi (r.a.) says that it is not improbable that each of these five testaments is repeated ten times each day. Yet, to repeat them one hundred times is better.",
    "Tahlilaat (hymns of God's unity)\nIt is recommended to say the following doxology (zikr), which is reported from Imam Ali Ameer al-Momineen (a.s.), on the first ten days of Zilhajj. An excellent reward has been reported for those saying this doxology (zikr), which should preferably be repeated ten times a day:\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ اللَّيَالِيْ وَ الدُّهُوْرِ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO A'DADAL LAYAALEE WAD DOHOORE \nThere is no god save Allah as many as nights and ages. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ اَمْوَاجِ الْبُحُوْرِ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO A'DADA AMWAAJIL BOHOORE \nThere is no god save Allah as many as the waves of oceans. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَ رَحْمَتُهٗ خَيْرٌ مِمَّا يَجْمَعُوْنَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO WA RAHMATOHU KHAYRUN MIMMAA YAJ-MA-O'ONA \nThere is no god save Allah and His mercy is better than what they amass. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ الشَّوْكِ وَ الشَّجَرِ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO A'DADASH SHAWKE WASH SHAJARE \nThere is no god save Allah as many as thorns and trees. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ الشَّعْرِ وَ الْوَبَرِ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO A'DADASH SHA’RE WAL WABARE \nThere is no god save Allah as many as hairs and piles. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ الْحَجَرِ وَ الْمَدَرِ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO A'DADAL HAJARE WAL MADARE\nThere is no god save Allah as many as stones and loams. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ لَمْحِ الْعُيُوْنِ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO A'DADA LAMHIL O'YOONE \nThere is no god save Allah as many as sights of eyes. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ فِي اللَّيْلِ اِذَا عَسْعَسَ وَ الصُّبْحِ اِذَا تَنَفَّسَ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO FIL LAYLE EZAA A'S-A'SA WA FISH SUBHE EZAA TANAFFASA \nThere is no god save Allah in the night when it departs and in the morning when it brightens. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عَدَدَ الرِّيَاحِ فِي الْبَرَارِيْ وَ الصُّخُوْرِ \nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO A'DADAR REYAAHE FIL BARAAREE WAS-SOKHOORE \nThere is no god save Allah as much as wind in lands and rocks. \nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مِنَ الْيَوْمِ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُنْفَخُ فِي الصُّوْرِ.\nLAA ELAAHA ILLAL LAAHO MENAL YAWME ELAA YAWMIN YUNFAKHO FIS SOORE.\nThere is no god save Allah from this day up to the day when the Trumpet will be blown."
  ],
